/Author (Oxana Semyachkina\055Glushkovskaya\054 Thomas Penzel\054 Mikhail Poluektov\054 Ivan Fedosov\054 Maria Tzoy\054 Andrey Terskov\054 Inna Blokhina\054 Viktor Sidorov and J\374rgen Kurths)
/CreationDate (D\07220230630200112\05308\04700\047)
/Creator (LaTeX with hyperref)
/Keywords (Alzheimer\220s disease\073 phototherapy\073 sleep\073 photostimulation\073 mechanisms\073 brainlymphatic system\073 brain drainage\073 beta amyloid\073 smart sleep technologies\073 neurodegenerative diseases)
/ModDate (D\07220230630153757\05302\04700\047)
/Producer (pdfTeX\0551\05640\05621)
/Subject (The global number of people with Alzheimer\220s disease \050AD\051 doubles every 5 years\056 It has been established that unless an effective treatment for AD is found\054 the incidence of AD will triple by 2060\056 However\054 pharmacological therapies for AD have failed to show effectiveness and safety\056 Therefore\054 the search for alternative methods for treating AD is an urgent problem in medicine\056 The lymphatic drainage and removal system of the brain \050LDRSB\051 plays an important role in resistance to the progression of AD\056 The development of methods for augmentation of the LDRSB functions may contribute to progress in AD therapy\056 Photobiomodulation \050PBM\051 is considered to be a non\055pharmacological and safe approach for AD therapy\056 Here\054 we highlight the most recent and relevant studies of PBM for AD\056 We focus on emerging evidence that indicates the potential benefits of PBM during sleep for modulation of natural activation of the LDRSB at nighttime\054 providing effective removal of metabolites\054 including amyloid\055\054 from the brain\054 leading to reduced progression of AD\056 Our review creates a new niche in the therapy of brain diseases during sleep and sheds light on the development of smart sleep technologies for neurodegenerative diseases\056)
/Title (Phototherapy of Alzheimer\220s Disease\072 Photostimulation of Brain Lymphatics during Sleep\072 A Systematic Review)
>>
endobj
